The B6 path applied and ACKed the checkpoint record, created a format-1 checkpoint, then applied and ACKed the cut record through the active source adapter and retained its current protected cut. A separate no-ACK recovery cursor sought after the checkpoint and replayed into an isolated Store copy under an 8-record, 1 MiB, 30-second turn budget. It reached the protected cut after exactly one applied tail record. The original checkpoint still reported 10/0 and its original ACTIVE pointer was byte-for-byte unchanged. A fresh no-ACK cursor then observed the post-cut record at 10/2; replay did not apply it.

The smoke's successor accepts only the immediate next entry or batch member within one Pulsar ledger. It rejects ledger changes and therefore does not prove cross-ledger continuity. This run covers one local standalone Broker and one same-ledger path. Full legacy-state dispositions/readiness report, cross-ledger successor proof, durable cutover/activation, rollback, legacy reader retirement, central validation, and production authority remain open. B6 remains IN_PROGRESS / PENDING_CENTRAL_VALIDATION.

